nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\nexec python3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/scientific_evidence.py\" \"$@\"\nimport hashlib\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\nfrom jsonschema import validate\nfrom pypdf import PdfReader\n\n\ndef digest(path):\n    return hashlib.sha256(Path(path).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef main():\n  set -e\n  if [ -f \"$RECORDER_FILE\" ]; then\n    python3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" recorder \\\n      --paper-dir \"$PAPER_DIR\" --fls \"$RECORDER_FILE\"\n  elif [ \"$return_code\" -eq 0 ]; then\n    echo \"LaTeX recorder output missing: $PAPER_DIR/$RECORDER_FILE\" >&2\n    return 1\n  fi\n  return \"$return_code\"\n}\n\nrun_pdflatex\npython3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" bibtex \\\n  --paper-dir \"$PAPER_DIR\" --aux \"$AUX_FILE\"\nrun_sanitized bibtex \"$BASE\"\nrun_pdflatex\nrun_pdflatex\npython3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_rendered_si.py\" --pdf \"${BASE}.pdf\"\n193:Recorded cluster-resampling intervals for the policy contrasts, together with the complete rule--ceiling grid, appear in Supplementary Information. The intervals retain the unit of resampling used by the evaluator and are not reassigned to the cross-rule contrast. No controlled component ablation supports a mechanistic attribution to a proposed optimization refinement. The measured exact-versus-greedy difference is sufficient for the limited selection-policy conclusion.\n202:The final evaluation is completed and qualified, with recorded control pass fraction $1.0$. Qualification concerns the evaluator's supported claims and specified consistency checks, not optimality of every large-panel witness or unbiasedness of the post-selected scientific framing. Candidate-supplied diagnostics remain unverified; our measurements use recorded evaluator decisions and inspectable source instead. There is no failed final qualification to reinterpret as a performance result. The absence of a qualifying alternative in development does not invalidate the completed frozen comparison, and neither fact establishes general superiority.\n232:\\bibliography{references}\n233:\\bibliographystyle{iclr2026_conference}\n237:\\section{Supplementary Information}\n479:Constant-ceiling controls provide no strict winner. Zero-response controls cannot improve a nonleader. Joint nonidentity column permutations test semantic-coordinate consistency, and reset replay checks repeatability of logical outputs. Recorded control pass fraction is $1.0$ and final qualification is completed and qualified. These checks are narrow behavioral checks; they do not certify real training effects, independent datasets, absence of every adaptive choice, or exactness of large-panel order-statistic solutions. The diagnostic trust field remains unverified and supplies no extra empirical claim.\n484:Development selection retained the reference procedure: three alternatives were scored, none unscored, no alternative met the recorded selection requirements, and the retained development-score change was zero. Those development outcomes are distinct from the independently completed final evaluation. The available feedback does not identify why the alternatives failed qualification; neither statistical underperformance nor a validity/adaptivity defect is asserted as the sole cause. No missing performance evidence is counted as a measured loss. These unsuccessful comparisons do not constitute controlled component ablations.\n490:\\subsection{LLM Usage}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
