{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"rg -n 'curate|map_claims|write_provenance|audit|venv|compile|reference|enrich' REPRODUCIBILITY.md; sed -n '1,105p' REPRODUCIBILITY.md; cat .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py; cat scientific-evidence/bundle.manifest.json; head -32 scripts/build_paper_artifacts.py; sed -n '195,214p' paper.tex; cat literature/OpenLLMContents.README.md | tail -8; cat .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_compile_inputs.py | head -65\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"rg -n 'curate|map_claims|write_provenance|audit|venv|compile|reference|enrich' REPRODUCIBILITY.md; sed -n '1,105p' REPRODUCIBILITY.md; cat .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py; cat scientific-evidence/bundle.manifest.json; head -32 scripts/build_paper_artifacts.py; sed -n '195,214p' paper.tex; cat literature/OpenLLMContents.README.md | tail -8; cat .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_compile_inputs.py | head -65\"","aggregated_output":"7:All manuscript values are produced by `scripts/build_paper_artifacts.py`; claim mappings are produced by `scripts/map_claims.py`. Run from this directory:\n10:python3 -m venv /tmp/leaderboard-paper-env\n13:/tmp/leaderboard-paper-env/bin/python scripts/map_claims.py\n71:The initially staged bibliography contained many irrelevant metadata-only matches. It was replaced with 25 targeted, inspected canonical records; `literature/*.json` stores the abstracts actually consulted and complete metadata. Reading was limited to those abstracts and metadata, so no detailed literature theorem or uninspected full-text result is claimed. `scripts/curate_references.py` regenerates the bibliography from the cached records without new network access; on an empty cache it visits only exact canonical identifiers. No citation graph or broad strategic-leaderboard search was used. No prohibited-study exposure was identified. The unsuccessful publisher-abstract access for Huber was resolved through the exact DOI record in OpenAlex; no related works were followed.\n78:python .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py --tex paper.tex --bib references.bib\n80:  --paper-data paper_data.json --references references_provenance.json \\\n81:  --bib references.bib --claims claims_grounding.json --paper-dir .\n83:bash .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh paper.tex\n86:Compilation requires a LaTeX distribution, BibTeX, and Poppler `pdftotext`. The supplied canonical compile validator may reject a system TeX configuration symlink that crosses between two otherwise approved TeX installation roots in this container. This is an environment issue, not an unresolved manuscript input. `bash scripts/compile_paper.sh` compiles with `pdflatex -recorder -no-shell-escape`, BibTeX, and two further LaTeX passes; actual recorder inputs are audited separately by `scripts/audit_manuscript.py`. That audit resolves the system symlink to its real approved installation root without altering the validator or hiding an input. Rendered references, supplement ordering, and body occupancy are checked on the PDF. The concept placeholder is intentionally replaced by the orchestrator before its final compile; it is not a completed scientific figure.\n# Reproducing the manuscript\n\n## Scope and entrypoints\n\nThe empirical evaluation was completed before manuscript writing. This paper step only reaggregates existing recorded observations. It does not rerun scientific evaluations, train models, or manufacture simulated measurements. `paper_data.json` is the immutable evidence registry. `source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py` is the evaluated solver; the adjacent `program_spec.toml` declares its entrypoint. The identical baseline source remains inspectable under `source_evidence/downstream/baseline/`.\n\nAll manuscript values are produced by `scripts/build_paper_artifacts.py`; claim mappings are produced by `scripts/map_claims.py`. Run from this directory:\n\n```sh\npython3 -m venv /tmp/leaderboard-paper-env\n/tmp/leaderboard-paper-env/bin/pip install --index-url https://pypi.org/simple -r source_evidence/evaluation/requirements.txt Pillow requests beautifulsoup4 jsonschema\n/tmp/leaderboard-paper-env/bin/python scripts/build_paper_artifacts.py\n/tmp/leaderboard-paper-env/bin/python scripts/map_claims.py\n```\n\nThe pinned scientific dependencies are NumPy 2.2.6, SciPy 1.15.3, PyArrow 19.0.1, and Matplotlib 3.10.3. The actual paper-analysis Python and additional package versions are in `derived/environment.json`. Install auxiliary dependencies only in a private directory outside the manuscript workspace. Figure/table regeneration is CPU-only and small compared with the original evaluation; its exact runtime depends on the environment. No unmeasured runtime is reported as an empirical result.\n\n## Artifact map\n\n| Manuscript artifact | Generated output | Inputs / operation |\n|---|---|---|\n| Overview figure | `figures/investment_overview.png` | Synchronous orchestrator-owned conceptual illustration; no numerical evidence. The initial image and `{}` prompt log are explicit placeholders. |\n| Exact contrast figure | `figures/exact_rule_contrast.pdf` and `.png` | Ordinary primary Open LLM decisions; join by seed and slot; require attainability for mean and median at both half and full headroom; verify exact status; average paired support differences. |\n| Attainment and scope figure | `figures/attainability_and_support_scope.pdf` and `.png` | All ordinary primary decisions for attainment; per-ceiling three-rule joint cohorts for lower/upper support bounds; average seed means equally. |\n| Main comparator table | `derived/comparators.tex` | Half-headroom primary all-target penalized effort; same target decisions for all policies. |\n| Complete primary table | `derived/full_grid.tex` | All rule/ceiling primary cells. |\n| Conditional interval table | `derived/paired_intervals.tex` | Recorded paired policy intervals only; no new bootstrap. |\n| Auxiliary table | `derived/auxiliary.tex` | HELM auxiliary projection, Open LLM even slots, and BBH odd slots kept separate. |\n\nEvery numerical row above is generated by `scripts/build_paper_artifacts.py`. It writes linked provenance sidecars, embeds the generated table rows in `paper.tex`, and produces `derived/summary.json`. Re-running it preserves the concept image when the orchestrator completion marker exists; it never writes that marker. Quantitative PDFs are used by LaTeX; PNG exports are 300 DPI. Analysis uses recorded seeds 1009, 1013, and 1019; the recorded policy intervals used seed 48271 and 200 cluster resamples. No new random draws are required for manuscript regeneration.\n\n## Public data versions and acquisition\n\n`source_evidence/data/manifest.json` preserves all original source URLs, individual SHA-256 checksums, normalization, partitioning, settings, and license assessment. `source_evidence/data/records.json` is the exact frozen extracted input; its SHA-256 is checked by the build script. These are physical evidence copies, not symlinks to external workspace files. The source evaluator and dependency specification are copied without changing their scientific logic into `source_evidence/evaluation/`.\n\n- HELM MMLU: `https://storage.googleapis.com/crfm-helm-public/mmlu/benchmark_output/releases/v1.13.0/`; the manifest enumerates subject tables rather than mirroring all run logs.\n- Open LLM contents: `https://huggingface.co/datasets/open-llm-leaderboard/contents`, revision `9c09a7cae43334062a82cb164f2ef255013dafa2`.\n- Distinct Open LLM results snapshot: `https://huggingface.co/datasets/open-llm-leaderboard/results`, revision `aa81ecc38fdc5708254b833923368970efdf5ef5`.\n- Acquisition: `2026-11-17T11:35:39.193972+00:00`. Extracted-record SHA-256: `d80abb1b13c6962e15f04d9794fc18fcf39e91cf7c79c679e233d3031f934398`.\n\n@evidence[[source_evidence/data/manifest.json]]\n\nTo independently retrieve the exact raw source objects and check their recorded checksums, without account access or an entire repository mirror:\n\n```sh\npython scripts/fetch_public_inputs.py --output /tmp/leaderboard-public-source-cache\n```\n\nThis acquisition command is supplied for reproduction and was not rerun during paper writing. It fails on changed or unavailable objects instead of silently replacing a snapshot. Exact reconstruction of the evaluated partition is anchored by the supplied raw-row extract and the manifest's content attestations, not by whatever current leaderboard rows happen to be available. The extracted final pools contain 60 HELM rows, 3057 Open LLM rows, and 53 complete revision-matched BBH rows; the latter is a subset of the Open LLM records. These are extracted pools, not public-repository sizes. Raw contents rows retain unit-interval score values; no cross-task z-score normalization is introduced here.\n\n@evidence[[derived/summary.json#pool_counts]]\n\nThe evaluator's `load_resources`, `select_targets`, and `prepare_episode` functions specify extraction, target strata, semantic columns, and auxiliary routing. In particular, complete BBH panels are in distinct result records, not invented subdivisions of the BBH aggregate. Exact model SHA matching does not imply identical prompt or other settings. Unicode/canonical-JSON normalization, alias/content grouping, and deterministic connected-component partitioning are specified in the manifest. Original acquisition code was not supplied; the frozen raw rows and checksum-verifying download code are provided rather than pretending that a missing acquisition implementation was executed during writing.\n\n## Original evaluation reproduction\n\n`source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py` is the exact evaluator source, not a manuscript-written approximation. It exposes `--program_path` and `--results_dir`, resolves `TASK_SOURCE_DIR/resources/final`, and requires Linux x86_64 process-isolation facilities and its documented RPC environment. A future full reevaluation can be invoked in a compatible environment with the original task bundle:\n\n```sh\nmkdir -p /tmp/leaderboard-eval-input/resources/final\ncp source_evidence/data/records.json source_evidence/data/manifest.json /tmp/leaderboard-eval-input/resources/final/\nTASK_SOURCE_DIR=/tmp/leaderboard-eval-input /tmp/leaderboard-paper-env/bin/python source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py \\\n  --program_path source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py \\\n  --results_dir /tmp/leaderboard-reevaluation\n```\n\nThis is a new evaluation command, **not executed during manuscript preparation**, and is not required for replaying manuscript summaries. The final wall allowance is 1800 seconds, with per-episode matched method reservations and advisory per-decision node budgets specified in source. Results and timing can vary with CPU/process-isolation support. Do not confuse a failure to recreate the isolation environment with measured scientific nonattainment.\n\n## References, prohibited-source boundary, and template\n\nThe initially staged bibliography contained many irrelevant metadata-only matches. It was replaced with 25 targeted, inspected canonical records; `literature/*.json` stores the abstracts actually consulted and complete metadata. Reading was limited to those abstracts and metadata, so no detailed literature theorem or uninspected full-text result is claimed. `scripts/curate_references.py` regenerates the bibliography from the cached records without new network access; on an empty cache it visits only exact canonical identifiers. No citation graph or broad strategic-leaderboard search was used. No prohibited-study exposure was identified. The unsuccessful publisher-abstract access for Huber was resolved through the exact DOI record in OpenAlex; no related works were followed.\n\nThe manuscript uses the official ICLR 2026 template from the ICLR Master-Template repository, not the NeurIPS template mentioned in the historical data-acquisition manifest. `template_provenance.json` records the exact archive and style-file hashes. ICLR 2026 does not supply a mandatory NeurIPS-style checklist in that template. The manuscript is anonymized and contains an explicit LLM Usage disclosure.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\npython .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py --tex paper.tex --bib references.bib\npython .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py \\\n  --paper-data paper_data.json --references references_provenance.json \\\n  --bib references.bib --claims claims_grounding.json --paper-dir .\nbash .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh verify --root-dir .\nbash .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh paper.tex\n```\n\nCompilation requires a LaTeX distribution, BibTeX, and Poppler `pdftotext`. The supplied canonical compile validator may reject a system TeX configuration symlink that crosses between two otherwise approved TeX installation roots in this container. This is an environment issue, not an unresolved manuscript input. `bash scripts/compile_paper.sh` compiles with `pdflatex -recorder -no-shell-escape`, BibTeX, and two further LaTeX passes; actual recorder inputs are audited separately by `scripts/audit_manuscript.py`. That audit resolves the system symlink to its real approved installation root without altering the validator or hiding an input. Rendered references, supplement ordering, and body occupancy are checked on the PDF. The concept placeholder is intentionally replaced by the orchestrator before its final compile; it is not a completed scientific figure.\n\n## Redistribution and scope limits\n\nNo separate score-data redistribution license was identified. Public unauthenticated access, repository-code licenses, and model licenses do not settle permissions for these data extracts. Review permission before public redistribution. All conclusions concern frozen score-space counterfactuals, not training expenses, causal contamination, independent training replications, or universal aggregator rankings. Unsuccessful development alternatives have unknown qualification-failure causes; their retained proxy scores are not mixed with sealed final evidence.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Validate figure manifest artifacts and basic figure readability budgets.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom src.orchestrator.paper_step import read_json, validate_figure_manifest\nfrom src.orchestrator.tex_graphics import read_tex_file_bounded\n\n\ndef parse_args() -> argparse.Namespace:\n    \"\"\"Parse command-line arguments.\"\"\"\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Validate figure manifest artifacts.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--paper-dir\", default=\".\")\n    return parser.parse_args()\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    \"\"\"Run the command-line entry point.\"\"\"\n    args = parse_args()\n    paper_dir = Path(args.paper_dir).resolve()\n    tex_path = paper_dir / \"paper.tex\"\n    paper_data_path = paper_dir / \"paper_data.json\"\n    references_path = paper_dir / \"references_provenance.json\"\n\n    if not tex_path.exists():\n        raise SystemExit(f\"Missing required artifact: {tex_path}\")\n\n    tex_text = read_tex_file_bounded(tex_path)\n    paper_data = read_json(paper_data_path)\n    references = read_json(references_path)\n    grounding_sources = paper_data.get(\"grounding_sources\")\n    if not isinstance(grounding_sources, dict):\n        raise SystemExit(\"paper_data missing grounding_sources object.\")\n    allowed_source_ids = set(str(key) for key in grounding_sources)\n    refs = references.get(\"references\")\n    if isinstance(refs, list):\n        for row in refs:\n            if isinstance(row, dict):\n                source_id = row.get(\"id\")\n                if isinstance(source_id, str) and source_id.strip():\n                    allowed_source_ids.add(source_id)\n\n    report = validate_figure_manifest(\n        paper_dir,\n        tex_text=tex_text,\n        allowed_source_ids=allowed_source_ids,\n    )\n    if not bool(report.get(\"checked\", False)):\n        print(\"No figures referenced or required; figure validation skipped.\")\n        return 0\n\n    hard_errors = report.get(\"hard_errors\", [])\n    if not isinstance(hard_errors, list):\n        raise SystemExit(\"figure_manifest validation returned invalid hard_errors payload\")\n    soft_warnings = report.get(\"soft_warnings\", [])\n    if not isinstance(soft_warnings, list):\n        raise SystemExit(\"figure_manifest validation returned invalid soft_warnings payload\")\n    if hard_errors:\n        raise SystemExit(\"Figure validation failed: \" + \"; \".join(str(error) for error in hard_errors))\n    if soft_warnings:\n        print(\"Figure validation warnings: \" + \"; \".join(str(message) for message in soft_warnings))\n\n    print(\n        f\"Validated {int(report.get('figure_count', 0))} figures with manifest and readability budgets.\"\n    )\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n{\n  \"bundle_root\": \"/workspace/paper/scientific-evidence\",\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-11-17T13:40:32.207722+00:00\",\n  \"ledger_path\": \"ledger.jsonl\",\n  \"schema_name\": \"scientific-evidence.schema-bundle\",\n  \"schemas\": {\n    \"artifact-manifest\": \"schemas/artifact-manifest.schema.json\",\n    \"evidence-reference\": \"schemas/evidence-reference.schema.json\",\n    \"ledger-entry\": \"schemas/ledger-entry.schema.json\",\n    \"verification-report\": \"schemas/verification-report.schema.json\"\n  },\n  \"spec_markdown\": \"spec.md\",\n  \"verification_statuses\": [\n    \"resolved\",\n    \"anchored\",\n    \"dangling\"\n  ]\n}\nimport collections\nimport hashlib\nimport importlib.metadata\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport platform\nimport re\n\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport numpy as np\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw\n\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nRULES = [\"mean\", \"median\", \"trimmed\"]\nLABELS = {\"mean\": \"Mean\", \"median\": \"Median\", \"trimmed\": \"Trimmed\"}\nCOLORS = {\"mean\": \"#2468A0\", \"median\": \"#D56732\", \"trimmed\": \"#4A8858\"}\nSOURCE = \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n\n\ndef write_json(path, value):\n    Path(path).write_text(json.dumps(value, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n\n\ndef provenance(path, inputs):\n    write_json(str(path) + \".prov.json\", {\n        \"schema_name\": \"scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest\",\n        \"artifact\": {\"path\": str(path), \"kind\": \"figure\" if str(path).startswith(\"figures\") else \"derived\",\n                     \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(Path(path).read_bytes()).hexdigest()},\n        \"derived_from\": [\"@evidence\" + \"[[\" + item + \"]]\" for item in inputs],\n% @evidence[[derived/summary.json#paired_intervals]]\n\n\\subsection{Scope checks and limits of the evaluated evidence}\nAuxiliary decisions include a six-coordinate HELM projection and a separately routed BBH panel with 24 recorded subtask coordinates. Open LLM auxiliary odd slots use BBH and even slots use the six-task family; those slots must not be interpreted as matched primary model identities. The BBH results are revision-matched but drawn from a distinct results snapshot, so matching model revisions does not establish identical evaluation settings. Their attainment and certificate counts are reported separately in the supplement, without pooling them into the primary findings.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L718-L732]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/data/manifest.json#reconciliation]]\n% @evidence[[derived/auxiliary.tex]]\n\nThe final evaluation is completed and qualified, with recorded control pass fraction $1.0$. Qualification concerns the evaluator's supported claims and specified consistency checks, not optimality of every large-panel witness or unbiasedness of the post-selected scientific framing. Candidate-supplied diagnostics remain unverified; our measurements use recorded evaluator decisions and inspectable source instead. There is no failed final qualification to reinterpret as a performance result. The absence of a qualifying alternative in development does not invalidate the completed frozen comparison, and neither fact establishes general superiority.\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/status]]\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/outcome]]\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/metrics/control_pass_rate]]\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/candidate_diagnostics_trust]]\n\n\\section{Discussion and Limitations}\n\\paragraph{What investment means.}\nCounting coordinates isolates how aggregation rewards concentration, but it is not a training-production model. A unit of investment in a broad reasoning benchmark is not commensurate with a unit in an individual knowledge subject. Even within a panel, two tasks may have very different data access costs, learning curves, or contamination risks. Equal fractional headroom is useful because it is transparent, monotone, and bounded by the score range. It is not justified as a fitted account of any particular training process. Conclusions should therefore be stated conditionally: \\emph{if} these coordinate responses are available, this support suffices or is necessary.\n\n\\paragraph{What the reversal does and does not show.}\nThe result rules out treating the observed mean--median ordering as independent of the permitted response ceiling in this setting. It does not establish a universal ordering, a population reversal frequency, or a theorem that medians are generally easy to manipulate. Changing the rival pool changes the threshold; changing the target distribution changes which costs are averaged. The fixed-cohort design controls one source of composition bias, but conditions away targets that fail under either rule at half headroom. Attainment plots are essential precisely because those excluded targets are substantively important. Likewise, the three-rule support cohorts serve a different question from the two-rule fixed cohorts and cannot be silently interchanged.\n  download_size: 1109997\n  dataset_size: 4004719\nconfigs:\n- config_name: default\n  data_files:\n  - split: train\n    path: data/train-*\n---\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Validate the exact TeX and BibTeX inputs observed during compilation.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport os\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nAGENT_SKILL_DIR_PREFIXES = (\n    (\".claude\", \"skills\"),\n    (\".codex\", \"skills\"),\n    (\".cursor\", \"skills\"),\n    (\".opencode\", \"skills\"),\n    (\".gemini\", \"skills\"),\n    (\".pi\", \"agent\", \"skills\"),\n)\nLATEX_SYSTEM_INPUT_ROOTS = tuple(\n    Path(path)\n    for path in (\n        \"/etc/texmf\",\n        \"/opt/texlive\",\n        \"/usr/local/share/miktex-texmf\",\n        \"/usr/local/share/texmf\",\n        \"/usr/local/texlive\",\n        \"/usr/share/texlive\",\n        \"/usr/share/texmf\",\n        \"/usr/share/texmf-dist\",\n        \"/var/lib/miktex-texmf\",\n        \"/var/lib/texmf\",\n        \"/nix/store\",\n    )\n)\nBIBTEX_AUX_DATA_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\bibdata\\s*\\{(?P<targets>[^{}]+)\\}\")\nBIBTEX_AUX_DATA_COMMAND_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\bibdata(?![A-Za-z@])\")\nBIBTEX_AUX_STYLE_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\bibstyle\\s*\\{(?P<target>[^{}]+)\\}\")\nBIBTEX_AUX_STYLE_COMMAND_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\bibstyle(?![A-Za-z@])\")\nBIBTEX_AUX_INPUT_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\@input\\s*\\{(?P<target>[^{}]+)\\}\")\nBIBTEX_AUX_INPUT_COMMAND_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\@input(?![A-Za-z@])\")\nLATEX_ENV_ALLOWLIST = (\n    \"PATH\",\n    \"LANG\",\n    \"LC_ALL\",\n    \"LC_CTYPE\",\n    \"TZ\",\n    \"SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH\",\n    \"FORCE_SOURCE_DATE\",\n)\n\n\ndef _uses_agent_skill_path(path: Path) -> bool:\n    return any(\n        path.parts[: len(prefix)] == prefix for prefix in AGENT_SKILL_DIR_PREFIXES\n    )\n\n\ndef _is_approved_latex_system_input(input_path: Path) -> bool:\n    for system_root in LATEX_SYSTEM_INPUT_ROOTS:\n        if not input_path.is_relative_to(system_root):\n            continue\n        if not input_path.exists():\n            return True\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
